  "worked_solution": "We're given the **rate of change** in population $r(t).$ To find the change in  population between  $2010$ and $2015$, we integrate $r(t)$ between the$t=5$ and $t=10.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{10}200{e}^{0.2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =200\\cdot {{e}^{0.2t}|}_{5}^{10} \\\\  & =1\\,000\\,{{e}^{0.2t}|}_{5}^{10} \\\\  & =1\\,000({e}^{2}-{e}^{1}) \\\\  & \u22484\\,671\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.  \n\nTherefore, between  $2010$ and $2015$ the population of the town increased by $4\\,671$ people.",
